/*
 * $DOC$
 * $NAME$
 * GTI_WINDOWBORDERED
 *
 * $ONELINER$
 * Query or change whether the window has a frame
 *
 * $SYNTAX$
 * GtInfo( GTI_WINDOWBORDERED, [lBordered] ) --> lBordered
 *
 * $ARGUMENTS$
 * `GTI_WINDOWBORDERED` The selector, from gtinfo.ch.
 * `lBordered` .T. shows the title bar and the frame, .F. hides them.
 *
 * $RETURNS$
 * The setting before the call.
 *
 * $DESCRIPTION$
 * The text area keeps its place and size on the desktop, so the screen contents stay.
 *
 * $NOTES$
 * Supported by GTWVT, GTSDL3, GTXWC and GTGLFW. On other terminals the result is NIL.
 *
 * $EXAMPLES$
 *
 * $OUTPUT$
 *
 * $CATEGORY$
 * Functions GT
 *
 * $HEADER$
 * gtinfo.ch
 *
 * $SEEALSO$
 * GTI_WINDOWALWAYSONTOP, GTI_ISFULLSCREEN
 *
